.\" Manpage for ubuntu-app-control
.TH UBUNTU-APP-CONTROL 1 "2026-10-22" "2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ubuntu-app-control \- review installed apps, clear their data, and choose a GPU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ubuntu-app-control
.RI [ --version ]
.br
.B ubuntu-app-control
.B --scan-report
.RI [ --scan-details ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ubuntu-app-control
lists the applications available to the current user (Snaps, AppImages and
desktop packages) rather than the entire package list. For each app it reports
how much cache and personal data it owns and offers to:
.IP \(bu 2
empty cache folders in place, which frees disk space immediately;
.IP \(bu 2
move app data and settings into a restorable area instead of deleting them;
.IP \(bu 2
uninstall the app with PackageKit/polkit or move an AppImage to the Trash;
.IP \(bu 2
pin which graphics card launches an app by writing a per-user desktop entry.
.PP
Cleared data is stored under
.IR ~/.local/share/ubuntu-app-control/quarantine .
Use the
.B "Restore or delete data"
window to put it back or delete it permanently.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.B --scan-report
Print a text summary of the app scan without opening a window.
.TP
.B --scan-details
With
.BR --scan-report ,
print one line per discovered entry.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ubuntu-app-control/prefs.json
GPU choices and the quarantine manifest.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ubuntu-app-control/quarantine
App data waiting to be restored or deleted.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications
Per-user GPU launchers.
.SH SAFETY
The program only deletes or moves folders inside a fixed allow-list of
per-user data directories. It refuses symlinked or shared paths and asks for
confirmation before each destructive action. Privileged commands are resolved
from root-owned system directories before they are passed to
.BR pkexec (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snap (8),
.BR apt (8),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR desktop-file-validate (1)
